    _compact("CLN-D03", "sofa-smells-stains-cleaning", "Sofa smells or stains? Clean it without setting the mark", "Cleaning", "professional-cleaning", "A child drops kahwa on the beige sofa in the living room; an uncle reaches for rubbing powder before anyone can stop him.", "Blot fresh spills, identify the fabric tag, and test any cleaner in a hidden seam. Old odour, deep staining, or water-sensitive fabric is better handled by upholstery cleaning.", "A ring-shaped stain or stale smell", "Moisture or residue trapped in the upholstery", ["Tea, kahwa, milk, or oily snacks pushed deeper by rubbing.", "Damp cushions that never dried through.", "Too much soap left in fabric, which catches fresh dirt."], [("Blot, do not scrub", "a fresh spill", "Press a clean white cloth from edge toward the centre; do not rub it wider."), ("Read the care tag", "unknown fabric", "Check whether the sofa is water-safe before using a wet cleaner."), ("Spot-test a mild cleaner", "washable fabric", "Test a tiny hidden patch and let it dry before treating the mark."), ("Dry it properly", "a damp smell", "Use airflow and open cushions where possible; avoid soaking the foam."), ("Arrange upholstery extraction", "old stains or odour", "A pro can rinse residue and dry the filling without flooding it.")], "They lifted the kahwa ring without leaving a pale patch around it.", "Mehnaz, ", "In closed winter rooms, a sofa can stay damp far longer than it feels on top. A heater facing wet fabric can bake in a smell; airflow is kinder.", "Do not mix cleaners or saturate a sofa near electrical recliner parts.", "Book cleaning for old odour, large stains, pet accidents, mould spots, or delicate silk/velvet upholstery."),
    _compact("PNT-D01", "painting-damp-walls-kashmir", "Damp walls before painting? Fix the water, not just the colour", "Painting", "painting", "A fresh coat goes on a bedroom wall on Friday. By Monday, a brown tide mark has returned above the skirting.", "Do not paint over active damp. Trace the moisture source, let the wall dry, treat salts or mould safely, then repair and paint.", "Paint bubbles, flakes, or shows a brown patch", "Moisture behind the paint film", ["A leaking pipe or bathroom wall on the other side.", "Rain entry at a window, roof edge, or exterior crack.", "Cold-wall condensation behind furniture in winter."], [("Check whether the patch is active", "recent damp", "Tape a small foil square over the area overnight; moisture behind it suggests the wall is still wet."), ("Look across the wall", "hidden source", "Inspect the adjoining bathroom, window and exterior face before buying paint."), ("Move furniture away", "condensation marks", "Give cold walls breathing space and wipe condensation."), ("Repair and dry", "a confirmed leak", "Fix the source and allow real drying time, not just a warm surface."), ("Prime after preparation", "a dry repaired wall", "Use the appropriate stain-blocking or damp-treatment system after the wall is sound.")], "The painter refused to cover it first. The pipe leak was tiny but constant.", "Rafiq, ", "Snow, rain and cold exterior walls make damp diagnosis seasonal. A patch near a window is not automatically a plumbing leak.", "Do not trap mould under paint or use a room heater to hide an active leak.", "Book a painter or repair pro after the source is fixed; book urgently for spreading mould, a wet electrical point, or a ceiling bulge."),
    _compact("CRP-D01", "door-not-closing-properly", "Door not closing properly? Find the rub before forcing the latch", "Carpentry", "carpentry", "In a rain-swollen old house, the bedroom door needs a shoulder nudge every night. The latch is innocent; the frame has moved a little.", "Locate where the door rubs, tighten hinge screws, and check the latch alignment. Do not plane or force a door until you know whether moisture or a shifting frame caused it.", "Door rubs, sticks, or misses the latch", "Loose hinges, seasonal swelling, or frame movement", ["Wood swelling after damp weather.", "Loose hinge screws letting the door sag.", "A latch plate sitting a few millimetres out of line."], [("Mark the rub", "a sticking edge", "Close slowly and look for fresh scrape marks or use a pencil mark on the edge."), ("Tighten hinge screws", "a sagging door", "Use the correct screwdriver and check whether the top hinge is pulling away."), ("Check the strike plate", "latch misses", "See whether the latch hits above or below the plate before altering wood."), ("Ease only the right spot", "minor seasonal swelling", "A carpenter can shave a tiny marked edge and reseal it."), ("Inspect the frame", "a suddenly crooked gap", "Look for wall movement, damp timber, or a loose frame.")], "It was one loose top hinge screw, not a new door job.", "Yusuf, ", "Timber doors react to Kashmir's damp spells and dry heated rooms. A small gap in summer can become a rub after rain.", "Do not slam it, oil every part blindly, or plane a door that may be swollen from a leak.", "Book a carpenter for a cracked frame, persistent swelling, loose hinges in damaged wood, or a door that will not secure."),
    _compact("MSN-D01", "wall-cracks-cosmetic-structural", "Wall cracks: when is it paint-deep and when is it serious?", "Masonry", "masonry", "A thin line appears above a window in a rented flat. One person says paint it; another says the building is falling. Usually, neither verdict arrives from one glance.", "Hairline plaster cracks are often cosmetic, but wide, growing, diagonal, or displaced cracks need a mason or structural engineer. Photograph and measure before filling.", "A line in plaster or masonry", "Plaster movement, settlement, moisture, or structural movement", ["Seasonal movement and old plaster drying.", "Moisture weakening a wall or lintel area.", "Settlement or load movement around openings."], [("Photograph and date it", "any new crack", "Place a ruler beside it and take a clear photo for comparison."), ("Check width and direction", "triage", "Hairline paint cracks differ from widening diagonal cracks near doors or windows."), ("Look for matching clues", "possible movement", "Check sticking doors, fresh gaps, damp, and cracks on the other face."), ("Fix moisture first", "damp nearby", "Repair leaks or rain entry before patching plaster."), ("Get an assessment", "wide or growing cracks", "A qualified pro should inspect before cosmetic repair.")], "They measured it for a month; it stayed hairline and the repair was simple.", "Irfan, ", "Freeze-thaw, damp walls, and older masonry can reveal fine surface cracks in Kashmir. That does not make every crack harmless.", "Never chisel a crack wider to inspect it, hide a growing crack with putty, or joke away a ceiling crack.", "Book urgent inspection for a widening crack, sagging ceiling, bulge, displacement, fresh crack after shaking, or any crack with water and electrical points."),
    _compact("DRY-D02", "fabric-stains-dry-clean", "Which stains need dry cleaning—and which need a quick blot?", "Dry Cleaning", "dry-clean-laundry", "A wedding shawl catches a bright dab of wazwan gravy at home. The well-meaning aunt reaches for hot water; the fabric is already pleading for a calmer plan.", "Blot fresh stains, keep heat away, and read the care label. Silk, wool, embellished clothes, oil stains, and unknown marks should go to a dry cleaner with the stain identified.", "A visible stain on delicate fabric", "Oil, dye, protein, or tannin set into fibres", ["Hot water setting milk, egg, or blood stains.", "Rubbing spreading oil into wool or silk.", "Home bleach damaging colour or embroidery."], [("Read the label", "every special garment", "Check fibre and cleaning instructions before adding water."), ("Blot and lift solids", "fresh food spill", "Use a clean cloth; lift from the outside inward without scrubbing."), ("Keep it cool and unheated", "protein or unknown stain", "Do not iron, tumble-dry, or use hot water before treatment."), ("Tell the cleaner what happened", "professional treatment", "Name the stain, fabric, and any product already used."), ("Store it breathable", "before drop-off", "Keep the garment dry and loose, not folded wet in plastic.")], "They saved the pheran because we did not rub the oil in at home.", "Sana, ", "Pherans, shawls and wedding wear often mix wool, silk, lining and embroidery. One home remedy cannot safely treat all four.", "Do not use bleach on an unknown fabric, iron a stain, or leave a wet garment in a sealed bag.", "Book dry cleaning for silk, wool, suede, leather, embroidery, oil stains, old yellowing, and garments with a dry-clean-only label."),
    _compact("MEN-D04", "dandruff-itchy-scalp-men", "Dandruff and itchy scalp: stop scratching, start checking", "Men's Grooming", "mens-salon", "After a cap-heavy week, flakes show up on a black jacket before the meeting does. Scratching harder is not a treatment plan.", "Use a suitable anti-dandruff shampoo regularly, rinse fully, and avoid heavy oil on an inflamed scalp. Pain, pus, hair loss, or stubborn scaling needs a dermatologist.", "White flakes with itch", "Dandruff, product buildup, or irritated scalp", ["Infrequent washing after sweat and cap use.", "Heavy oil or styling product sitting on the scalp.", "A fungal or skin condition needing medical care."], [("Wash gently and regularly", "ordinary flakes", "Use lukewarm water and work shampoo onto scalp, not only hair."), ("Use an anti-dandruff shampoo correctly", "recurring dandruff", "Leave it on for the label time before rinsing."), ("Rinse product fully", "itch after styling", "Remove wax, gel and shampoo residue rather than layering more oil."), ("Clean caps and combs", "repeat flakes", "Wash items touching the scalp regularly."), ("Seek medical advice", "red flags", "Pain, pus, round hair loss or thick persistent plaques are not salon problems.")], "Changing the shampoo routine helped more than putting oil on it every night.", "Aamir, ", "Dry indoor heat can make scalp itch feel worse, while caps hold sweat close during travel. Both can coexist; neither needs aggressive scratching.", "Do not share combs, scratch until the skin breaks, or apply undiluted household ingredients to an inflamed scalp.", "Book grooming for routine scalp and hair care; see a dermatologist for infection signs, pain, marked hair loss, or no improvement after several weeks."),
    _compact("WMN-D04", "hair-damage-after-colour", "Hair damaged after colour? Pause the next chemical step", "Women's Salon", "womens-salon", "After a colour appointment before Eid, the ends of a woman's hair feel rougher than the new shade looks in the mirror. Another bleach session is not the rescue.", "Pause further bleach or colour, use gentle cleansing and conditioning, reduce heat, and trim splitting ends. A strand test and a skilled colourist matter before any corrective service.", "Dry, stretchy, rough, or breaking hair after colour", "Chemical and heat damage to the hair shaft", ["Bleach overlapping already-lightened hair.", "High heat on weakened ends.", "Skipping bond care and moisture after colour."], [("Pause chemical services", "new breakage", "Do not recolour immediately; damaged hair needs recovery time."), ("Wash gently", "dry rough hair", "Use a mild shampoo and conditioner, focusing conditioner on lengths."), ("Reduce heat", "fragile ends", "Air-dry when possible and use heat protection when styling."), ("Trim split ends", "fraying tips", "A small trim prevents splits travelling upward."), ("Ask for a strand test", "corrective colour", "A professional should test elasticity before promising a colour correction.")], "She told me to wait, test a strand, and trim first. That saved my length.", "Rukhsar, ", "Heated rooms make coloured lengths feel drier in winter, but more oil on the scalp will not repair a bleached end. Care needs to sit where the damage is.", "Do not bleach again at home, use a straightener daily on snapping hair, or pull through wet fragile hair.", "Book a colourist for corrective work, uneven bands, major breakage, or any service after a recent bleach."),
    _compact("GRD-D01", "lawn-looking-dead-kashmir", "Lawn looking dead after winter? Check if it is sleeping", "Gardening", "gardening", "In a quiet garden, the lawn looks like old rope after snow clears. The instinct is to drown it green; the grass may simply be waking slowly.", "Check whether grass crowns are alive, clear compacted debris, rake gently, and water only when the soil needs it. Patchy dead areas, pests, or poor drainage may need a gardener.", "Brown, thin lawn after cold weather", "Dormancy, compaction, poor drainage, or disease", ["Winter dormancy and delayed spring growth.", "Snow-matted leaves blocking light and air.", "Compacted soil or standing water around roots."], [("Test a small patch", "whether grass is alive", "Scratch near the crown; pale green growth suggests dormancy rather than death."), ("Rake gently", "matted debris", "Lift leaves and dead blades without tearing wet soil."), ("Check drainage", "soggy zones", "Notice where water stands after rain or snowmelt."), ("Water by soil feel", "dry spring weeks", "Water deeply only when the top soil is genuinely dry."), ("Patch and feed at the right time", "bare areas", "A gardener can match seed and timing to the local season.")], "We thought it was finished; the gardener said wait two weeks and clear the leaf mat.", "Tariq, ", "Kashmir lawns do not follow a hot-climate calendar. Snowmelt, shade from poplars, and compacted wet soil all change the spring answer.", "Do not scalp the lawn, overwater a cold wet patch, or throw fertiliser onto frozen soil.", "Book a gardener for persistent bare zones, fungal rings, pest damage, drainage problems, or an uneven lawn after the growth season begins."),
    _compact("ALU-D01", "aluminium-sliding-window-problems", "Aluminium sliding window stuck or leaking? Clean the track first", "Aluminium & Glass", "aluminium-steel-works", "A window in a flat starts scraping just as rain comes sideways. It is tempting to yank harder; the track is usually asking for grit removal, not a wrestling match.", "Vacuum the track, clear drain holes, inspect rollers and seals, then lubricate only with a suitable dry silicone product. Broken glass, loose frames, or persistent leaks need a window professional.", "Sliding panel drags, rattles, or lets rain in", "Grit in tracks, blocked weep holes, worn rollers, or failed seals", ["Dust and grit packed into the bottom track.", "Blocked drainage holes holding rainwater.", "Flattened weather seals or worn rollers."], [("Clean the track", "a dragging panel", "Vacuum grit, then wipe the channel with a soft brush and cloth."), ("Find weep holes", "rainwater in the frame", "Clear visible drainage openings gently; do not enlarge them."), ("Check the seal", "draught or leak", "Look for gaps, flattened rubber, and light around the closed panel."), ("Use dry silicone sparingly", "clean but sticky tracks", "Apply a window-safe dry lubricant, not thick oil that catches dust."), ("Have rollers adjusted", "persistent scraping", "A pro can align the panel without stressing glass.")], "Cleaning the little drain holes stopped the puddle on the sill.", "Sameer, ", "Wind-driven rain and winter dust are hard on sliding tracks. A clean track before the wet season prevents a surprising number of leaks.", "Do not force a jammed panel, drill random holes, or use heavy grease in a track.", "Book a pro for cracked glass, a loose panel, frame movement, persistent leakage, or a window that will not lock."),
    _compact("INT-D04", "false-ceiling-water-stain", "Water stain on a false ceiling? Treat it as a leak clue", "Interior Repair", "interior-decor", "A tea-coloured ring appears over the dining table at home. Everyone looks up at the ceiling; the leak may be above, next door, or at the roof edge.", "Do not repaint a water stain until the source is found and the ceiling is dry. Isolate nearby electricity and act fast if the board sags, feels soft, or drips.", "Brown ring, blister, or soft patch in false ceiling", "A leak above or old moisture trapped in the board", ["Bathroom or plumbing leak on the floor above.", "Roof or exterior water entry after rain.", "Condensation around a cold pipe or AC drain."], [("Check for active wetness", "new stain", "Touch only away from electrical fittings; note whether it is damp, growing, or dripping."), ("Protect the room", "active drip", "Move furniture and place a bucket without puncturing the board."), ("Isolate nearby power", "lights near stain", "Switch off the affected circuit and call an electrician if water is near fittings."), ("Find the source", "repair planning", "Inspect the room above, pipe runs, roof and exterior wall."), ("Repair and replace after drying", "a confirmed old leak", "A pro can remove damaged board, treat the area, and repaint only when dry.")], "The stain was from an AC drain pipe above, not a roof problem.", "Farah, ", "Snowmelt and roof seepage can travel along a slab before showing itself. The stain is a clue, not a map pin.", "Do not poke a sagging ceiling, repaint an active mark, or leave water near downlights.", "Book urgent repair for sagging board, dripping, mould smell, electrical fittings nearby, or a stain that grows after rain."),
    _compact("PET-D04", "dog-itching-scratching", "Dog itching and scratching? Check the skin, not just the fur", "Pet Care", "dog-grooming", "A dog in an apartment keeps scratching after every walk, then rubs his ears on the carpet. The family changes shampoo twice; the skin still needs a proper look.", "Check for fleas, redness, ear debris, and new products, but do not diagnose persistent itch at home. Gentle grooming helps; sores, ear pain, hair loss, or nonstop scratching need a veterinarian.", "Repeated scratching, licking, or rubbing", "Fleas, skin irritation, allergy, ear issue, or infection", ["Fleas or ticks hidden around the neck, tail base, or bedding.", "Damp coat and skin folds after walks or baths.", "Food, environmental, or product sensitivity."], [("Look without digging", "a mild new itch", "Part the coat in good light and check for fleas, redness, scabs, or damp skin."), ("Keep the coat dry", "after walks or baths", "Towel-dry thoroughly, especially ears, paws and folds."), ("Wash bedding", "possible flea exposure", "Clean bedding and vacuum resting spots; use vet-approved parasite control."), ("Use gentle grooming", "loose coat and dirt", "Brush carefully; stop if skin is sore or the dog reacts in pain."), ("See a veterinarian", "persistent or painful itch", "Skin infections and ear problems need diagnosis, not more shampoo.")], "The groomer spotted redness behind his ears and told us not to keep bathing him.", "Adeel, ", "Wet snow, muddy lanes and warm indoor rooms can leave a coat damp at the skin. Drying after walks is small work with a big payoff.", "Do not use human anti-dandruff shampoo, put oils on broken skin, or give human medicines.", "Book grooming for coat hygiene; see a vet promptly for wounds, bad odour, ear discharge, pain, hair loss, or persistent scratching."),
    _compact("VEH-D05", "car-ac-not-cooling", "Car AC not cooling? Do not start with a blind gas refill", "Vehicle Care", "car-repair-maintenance", "A family sits in afternoon traffic, AC on full, windows slowly cracking open anyway. The cabin fan is loud; the air is still warm.", "Confirm recirculation, fan and airflow first, then inspect the cabin filter and condenser area. Weak cooling can be a refrigerant leak, compressor issue, or blocked airflow; get a proper diagnosis before a refill.", "Car blower runs but cabin stays warm", "Dirty cabin filter, refrigerant loss, condenser blockage, or compressor fault", ["A clogged cabin air filter restricting cold airflow.", "Refrigerant leaked from a seal, hose, or condenser.", "Dust and debris blocking heat release at the condenser."], [("Set the correct mode", "a simple setting issue", "Use AC on with recirculation and close windows for a fair test."), ("Check cabin airflow", "weak vent flow", "A clogged cabin filter can make a cold system feel useless."), ("Look through the grille", "condenser debris", "Remove leaves and loose debris carefully; do not bend fins."), ("Listen for changes", "possible compressor issue", "Note unusual clicking, belt noise, or whether cooling changes with engine speed."), ("Request leak diagnosis", "warm air persists", "A workshop should test the system before adding refrigerant.")], "They changed the cabin filter and found the leak before charging it again.", "Danish, ", "Dusty summer roads and a car parked under poplars can load a condenser and cabin filter quickly. Test the AC before the first long family drive.", "Do not use leak-stop cans, overfill refrigerant, or spray water into engine electrical parts.", "Book vehicle care for no cooling after basic checks, oily hose marks, compressor noise, a visible leak, or a system that cools briefly then fades."),
